{"book":13,"chapter":30,"rubric":"PYTHON AS A FIRST LANGUAGE / METAPROGRAMMING / CHAPTER 30","slides":[{"title":"A program studies itself","sub":"Introspection and reflection","short":"Reflection","main":"An object can be asked what it is and what it can do.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Questions to an object","Tools","Where it's used"],"captions":["At run time a program can ask: what are you, what do you have, how do I call you?","type, dir, getattr, inspect.signature, getsource — the introspection toolkit","Debuggers, tests, docs, serialization, dependency injection — all rest on reflection"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"o","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":34.0,"text":"object","tone":"green","size":12.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":270.0,"y":38.0,"w":120.0,"h":22.0,"text":"what are you?","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":22.0,"text":"what do you have?","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":270.0,"y":102.0,"w":120.0,"h":22.0,"text":"how to call you?","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":146.0,"y1":62.0,"x2":208.0,"y2":40.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":146.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":208.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e3","x1":146.0,"y1":78.0,"x2":208.0,"y2":100.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t0","x":62.0,"y":54.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"type()","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t1","x":180.0,"y":54.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"dir()","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t2","x":298.0,"y":54.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"getattr()","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t3","x":62.0,"y":94.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"signature()","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t4","x":180.0,"y":94.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"getsource()","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t5","x":298.0,"y":94.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"currentframe()","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"t0","x":62.0,"y":50.0,"w":108.0,"h":26.0,"text":"debuggers","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t1","x":180.0,"y":50.0,"w":108.0,"h":26.0,"text":"tests","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t2","x":298.0,"y":50.0,"w":108.0,"h":26.0,"text":"docs","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t3","x":62.0,"y":90.0,"w":108.0,"h":26.0,"text":"serialization","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"t4","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":108.0,"h":26.0,"text":"dependency injection","tone":"blue","size":8.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[18.4,30.4]}]},{"title":"Types","sub":"type, mro, subclasses","short":"Types","main":"A base class finds its heirs itself.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Value type","__mro__","__subclasses__"],"captions":["type(x) is the value's class; isinstance respects inheritance, issubclass compares classes","__bases__ — direct parents, __mro__ — full name lookup order","__subclasses__() — known heirs: a base class finds plugins without a registry"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["type(3)              # int","isinstance(True, int)    # True","issubclass(bool, int)   # True"],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":290.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"bool","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"int","tone":"blue","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":290.0,"y":70.0,"w":80.0,"h":28.0,"text":"object","tone":"muted","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":112.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":138.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":222.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":248.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":118.0,"text":"bool.__mro__","size":10.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":180.0,"y":36.0,"w":100.0,"h":26.0,"text":"Plugin","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":100.0,"y":100.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":"JsonPlugin","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":260.0,"y":100.0,"w":90.0,"h":26.0,"text":"CsvPlugin","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":150.0,"y1":50.0,"x2":112.0,"y2":88.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":210.0,"y1":50.0,"x2":248.0,"y2":88.0,"tone":"blue","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":146.0,"text":"Plugin.__subclasses__()","size":10.0}]],"cues":[11.7,23.2]}]},{"title":"dir and vars","sub":"What's available vs. what's stored","short":"dir and vars","main":"dir is what's available, vars is what's stored here.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["dir","vars","Difference"],"captions":["dir(obj) — sorted list of all available names, inherited and special included","vars(obj) — dict of the instance's own attributes (obj.__dict__); objects with slots have none","dir answers \"what is available\", vars — \"what is stored right here\""],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["class P:","    def __init__(self): self.x = 1","    def move(self): ...","dir(P())   # ['__class__', ..., 'move', 'x']"],"hl":[3],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["p = P()","vars(p)    # {'x': 1}","p.__dict__ is vars(p)   # True"],"hl":[1],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":34.0,"text":"dir(obj)\neverything available","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":70.0,"w":120.0,"h":34.0,"text":"vars(obj)\nits own","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[13.2,23.2]}]},{"title":"Access by name","sub":"getattr and friends","short":"getattr","main":"Check names from outside.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["getattr","Command dispatcher","Careful"],"captions":["getattr(obj, name, default), setattr, hasattr, delattr — attribute access by string name","A user command becomes a method name: getattr(self, 'cmd_' + name)","A name from outside must not be used unchecked: a prefix or an allow-list is a must"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["getattr(p, 'x')","getattr(p, 'z', None)   # fallback","setattr(p, 'x', 5)","hasattr(p, 'move')"],"lang":"python","size":11.5,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["def run(self, name, *args):","    handler = getattr(self, 'cmd_' + name, None)","    if handler is None:","        raise ValueError(name)","    return handler(*args)"],"hl":[1],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["getattr(obj, user_input)   # dangerous","getattr(obj, 'cmd_' + user_input)"],"bad":[0],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":28.0,"w":310.0},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":130.0,"text":"check the name first","tone":"yellow","size":10.0}]],"cues":[15.5,30.6]}]},{"title":"Kinds of objects","sub":"inspect predicates","short":"Predicates","main":"callable says \"can be called\", inspect says \"what it is\".","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Predicates","Not by name","Why"],"captions":["inspect.isclass, isfunction, ismethod, iscoroutinefunction, isgeneratorfunction tell what you have","callable() only says whether it can be called; predicates tell the kinds apart","An async decorator, a class serializer, tests only for functions — all need to tell kinds apart"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"b0","x":56.0,"y":50.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"isclass","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b1","x":181.0,"y":50.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"isfunction","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b2","x":306.0,"y":50.0,"w":104.0,"h":26.0,"text":"ismethod","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b3","x":56.0,"y":90.0,"w":118.0,"h":26.0,"text":"iscoroutinefunction","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b4","x":181.0,"y":90.0,"w":118.0,"h":26.0,"text":"isgeneratorfunction","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":40.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["callable(len)            # True","callable(Point)          # True","inspect.isclass(Point)   # True","inspect.isclass(len)     # False"],"hl":[2,3],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"async decorator","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":90.0,"y":100.0,"w":130.0,"h":28.0,"text":"test runner","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"iscoroutinefunction","tone":"green","size":8.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"d","x":270.0,"y":100.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"isfunction","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":156.0,"y1":60.0,"x2":208.0,"y2":60.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":156.0,"y1":100.0,"x2":208.0,"y2":100.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[17.9,22.9]}]},{"title":"signature","sub":"Signature and bind","short":"signature","main":"A signature and call binding underpin checks and injection.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Signature","Parameter kinds","bind"],"captions":["inspect.signature(func) — signature: parameters, defaults, annotations","Parameter kinds: POSITIONAL_ONLY, POSITIONAL_OR_KEYWORD, VAR_POSITIONAL, KEYWORD_ONLY, VAR_KEYWORD","sig.bind(*args, **kw) binds a call to the signature or raises TypeError — basis of checks and dependency injection"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["def f(a, /, b, c=1, *args, d, **kw): ...","sig = inspect.signature(f)","# (a, /, b, c=1, *args, d, **kw)"],"hl":[1],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":64.0,"y":30.0,"w":70.0,"h":22.0,"text":"a","tone":"blue","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k0","x":210.0,"y":30.0,"w":140.0,"h":22.0,"text":"POSITIONAL_ONLY","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":64.0,"y":58.0,"w":70.0,"h":22.0,"text":"b, c","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k1","x":210.0,"y":58.0,"w":140.0,"h":22.0,"text":"POS_OR_KW","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":64.0,"y":86.0,"w":70.0,"h":22.0,"text":"*args","tone":"yellow","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k2","x":210.0,"y":86.0,"w":140.0,"h":22.0,"text":"VAR_POSITIONAL","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":64.0,"y":114.0,"w":70.0,"h":22.0,"text":"d","tone":"violet","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k3","x":210.0,"y":114.0,"w":140.0,"h":22.0,"text":"KEYWORD_ONLY","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n4","x":64.0,"y":142.0,"w":70.0,"h":22.0,"text":"**kw","tone":"red","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"k4","x":210.0,"y":142.0,"w":140.0,"h":22.0,"text":"VAR_KEYWORD","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["bound = sig.bind(1, 2, d=4)","bound.apply_defaults()","bound.arguments","# {'a': 1, 'b': 2, 'c': 1, 'args': (), 'd': 4, 'kw': {}}"],"hl":[2],"lang":"python","size":9.5,"lh":24.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[13.4,32.9]}]},{"title":"Function attributes","sub":"Code and closures","short":"Functions","main":"__code__ and __closure__ reveal how a function is built.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Name and docs","__code__","__closure__"],"captions":["A function is an object: __name__, __qualname__, __doc__, __module__, __defaults__, __annotations__","__code__ holds the compiled body: co_argcount, co_varnames, co_consts, co_freevars","__closure__ holds cells of captured variables: cell_contents shows what a nested function carried off"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["f.__name__       # 'f'","f.__qualname__   # 'outer.<locals>.f'","f.__doc__","f.__defaults__   # (1,)"],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":24.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["code = f.__code__","code.co_argcount    # 2","code.co_varnames    # ('a', 'b', 'tmp')","code.co_freevars    # ('k',)"],"hl":[1,2,3],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":24.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":40.0,"lines":["def make(k):","    def f(x): return x * k","    return f","f = make(3)","f.__closure__[0].cell_contents   # 3"],"hl":[4],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":22.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[12.0,28.8]}]},{"title":"Source and frames","sub":"getsource, currentframe","short":"Frames","main":"Delete frame references after use.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["getsource","Frames","Who called"],"captions":["inspect.getsource, getfile, getdoc read the definition; console and exec objects have no source","inspect.currentframe() — current function's frame; f_back is its caller's frame","This is how a logger learns where it was called from; delete frame references after use — else cycles and memory"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["inspect.getsource(f)   # text of def","inspect.getfile(f)     # path to .py","inspect.getdoc(f)      # help text"],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":40.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"main()","tone":"muted","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":70.0,"y":80.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"handler()","tone":"muted","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":70.0,"y":120.0,"w":100.0,"h":24.0,"text":"log()  ← frame","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":70.0,"y1":106.0,"x2":70.0,"y2":94.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":70.0,"y1":66.0,"x2":70.0,"y2":54.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":250.0,"y":80.0,"text":"f_back →\nf_code.co_name\nf_lineno","size":10.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":24.0,"y":44.0,"lines":["def log(msg):","    frame = inspect.currentframe().f_back","    name = frame.f_code.co_name","    print(f'[{name}] {msg}')","    del frame"],"hl":[1,2,4],"lang":"python","size":10.0,"lh":22.0,"w":330.0}]],"cues":[12.1,33.2]}]},{"title":"Annotations","sub":"Reading types","short":"Annotations","main":"Read annotations with standard functions, not the dict.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["__annotations__","get_type_hints","annotationlib"],"captions":["A function or class has an annotations dict, but it may hold strings","typing.get_type_hints turns them into real types","Python 3.14 evaluates annotations lazily — annotationlib was added for reading; don't read the dict directly"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["def f(a: int, b: 'Point') -> str: ...","f.__annotations__","# {'a': int, 'b': 'Point', 'return': str}"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["typing.get_type_hints(f)","# {'a': int, 'b': Point, 'return': str}","# strings turned into types"],"hl":[0],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"get_type_hints","tone":"green","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":120.0,"h":28.0,"text":"annotationlib","tone":"yellow","size":10.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"standard functions, not the dict","size":10.0}]],"cues":[9.6,23.4]}]},{"title":"Modules","sub":"importlib","short":"Modules","main":"Plugins are found by names and entry points.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Import by name","Loaded","Plugins"],"captions":["importlib.import_module('pkg.mod') loads a module from a string — the name can come from settings","sys.modules — already loaded ones; a module has __name__ and __file__","Plugins: pkgutil lists submodules, importlib.metadata reads entry points — no explicit list"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["mod = importlib.import_module('json')","func = getattr(mod, 'dumps')","func({'a': 1})"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["'json' in sys.modules","json.__name__    # 'json'","json.__file__    # path to the file"],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":70.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"package\nplugins/","tone":"blue","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":190.0,"y":70.0,"w":100.0,"h":30.0,"text":"iter_modules","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c~cell","x":306.0,"y":70.0,"w":90.0,"h":30.0,"text":"import_module","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"line","id":"e1","x1":120.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":140.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"green","arrow":true,"width":1.6},{"t":"line","id":"e2","x1":240.0,"y1":70.0,"x2":262.0,"y2":70.0,"tone":"yellow","arrow":true,"width":1.6}]],"cues":[15.4,24.2]}]},{"title":"Uses","sub":"Where it's needed","short":"Uses","main":"All the information already lives in objects.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Representation","Configuration","Frameworks"],"captions":["A generic __repr__ and class-to-dict serialization are built from vars and fields","Tests are found by the test_ prefix, a command line is built from a function's signature","Dependency injection: the framework reads your function's parameters and annotations and decides what to pass"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["def to_dict(obj):","    return dict(vars(obj))","to_dict(p)   # {'x': 1, 'y': 2}"],"hl":[1],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["for name in dir(module):","    if name.startswith('test_'):","        getattr(module, name)()"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":310.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":50.0,"lines":["def handler(db: Database, user: User): ...","# framework: signature(handler)","# → find Database and User, pass them in"],"hl":[1,2],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":320.0}]],"cues":[12.0,22.6]}]},{"title":"Pitfalls","sub":"Careful","short":"Pitfalls","main":"A direct call is easier to debug.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Mangled names","Built-ins in C","Explicit is better"],"captions":["A name __secret in a class is mangled to _Class__secret — read it under the mangled name","Some C built-ins have no discoverable signature: signature raises ValueError","Reflection slows code and hurts readability — where a direct call is enough, use it"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["class A:","    __secret = 1","vars(A)   # '_A__secret'"],"hl":[2],"lang":"python","size":11.0,"lh":26.0,"w":300.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":30.0,"y":56.0,"lines":["inspect.signature(len)","inspect.signature(print)","# sometimes ValueError: no signature found"],"bad":[2],"lang":"python","size":10.5,"lh":26.0,"w":320.0}],[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":90.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"p.move()","tone":"green","size":11.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":270.0,"y":60.0,"w":130.0,"h":30.0,"text":"getattr(p, 'move')()","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"text","id":"n","x":180.0,"y":112.0,"text":"a direct call is easier to debug","size":10.0}]],"cues":[10.1,27.0]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"Introspection","short":"Summary","main":"type, dir, getattr, inspect, importlib.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Types","Attributes","inspect","Modules"],"captions":["type, isinstance, __mro__, __subclasses__ answer about types","dir and vars show attributes, getattr and setattr work with them by name","inspect tells kinds of objects apart, reads signature, source code and the call stack","import_module loads modules from a string — the basis of plugins and frameworks"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","